NNAAMMEE
     ggeetteenntt — get entries from administrative database

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ggeetteenntt _d_a_t_a_b_a_s_e [_k_e_y _._._.]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggeetteenntt utility retrieves and displays entries from the administrative
     database specified by _d_a_t_a_b_a_s_e, using the lookup order specified in
     nsswitch.conf(5).  The display format for a given _d_a_t_a_b_a_s_e is as per the
     “traditional” file format for that database.

     The _d_a_t_a_b_a_s_e argument may be one of:

           DDaattaabbaassee    DDiissppllaayy ffoorrmmaatt
           ethers      address name
           group       group:passwd:gid:[member[,member]...]
           hosts       address name [alias ...]
           netgroup    (host,user,domain) [...]
           networks    name network [alias ...]
           passwd      user:passwd:uid:gid:gecos:home_dir:shell
           protocols   name protocol [alias ...]
           rpc         name number [alias ...]
           services    name port/protocol [alias ...]
           shells      /path/to/shell
           utmpx       [time] type: properties

     If one or more _k_e_y arguments are provided, they will be looked up in
     _d_a_t_a_b_a_s_e using the appropriate function.  For example, “passwd” supports
     a numeric UID or user name; “hosts” supports an IPv4 address, IPv6 ad‐
     dress, or host name; and “services” supports a service name, service
     name/protocol name, numeric port, or numeric port/protocol name.

     If no _k_e_y is provided and _d_a_t_a_b_a_s_e supports enumeration, all entries for
     _d_a_t_a_b_a_s_e will be retrieved using the appropriate enumeration function and
     printed.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The ggeetteenntt utility exits 0 on success, 1 if there was an error in the
     command syntax, 2 if one of the specified key names was not found in
     _d_a_t_a_b_a_s_e, or 3 if there is no support for enumeration on _d_a_t_a_b_a_s_e.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Show entry for user sshd from the passwd database:

           $ getent passwd sshd
           sshd:*:22:22:Secure Shell Daemon:/var/empty:/usr/sbin/nologin

     Show entry for TCP from the protocols database:

           $ getent protocols tcp
           tcp                   6  TCP

     Show entry for the localhost IPv6 address ::1 from the hosts database:

           $ getent hosts ::1
           ::1               localhost  localhost.my.domain

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     getutxent(3), ethers(5), group(5), hosts(5), netgroup(5), networks(5),
     nsswitch.conf(5), passwd(5), protocols(5), rpc(5), services(5), shells(5)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     A ggeetteenntt command appeared in NetBSD 3.0, and was imported into
     FreeBSD 7.0.  It was based on the command of the same name in Solaris and
     Linux.

